Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-rs6000.c
Line: 2244
Function: xcoff_write_armap_big
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the 64-bit offsets loop, the inner while (map[i].abfd == iterator.current.member) does not check i < orl_count. If i reaches orl_count, the condition evaluates map[orl_count], resulting in an out-of-bounds array read.

